[h1]Living Fellows 0.26.67[/h1]

[b]Expeditions, Base Watch and Markus's taxi[/b]
[list]
[*]Collect wood expeditions: walk or drive to nearby woodland, borrow an axe, cut real trees and bring logs home. Choose a fixed amount or Full load, up to 256 logs and actual cargo capacity.
[*]Wood delivery tracks collected, carried and stored logs separately. Full storage pauses and retries; borrowed axes return to camp storage, including axes carried in bags.
[*]Keep the camp working while you travel with Base Watch, or send a squad to scout, search, fish or collect wood. The two share one companion view.
[*]Call Markus's taxi from a working walkie-talkie for a road pickup and a ride to a map destination.
[/list]

[b]Reliable work and travel[/b]
[list]
[*]Ordinary blocked camp jobs pause and retry automatically, with a countdown and manual Retry.
[*]Store searches have time to discover distant shelves before their search deadline.
[*]Wood preparation selects living crew after a leader handoff and follows the actual daylight policy. Car crews use safe short shuttles to nearby storage.
[*]Returning crews switch off their car. Solo-view recovery refreshes the primary player's lighting and wall cutaways.
[*]Base job controls are at the top of the Base tab, storage management is at the bottom, and policies use checkboxes.
[*]Log Yards fill neat four-log stacks in rows. Strange Folk can begin on day two, chosen randomly from eligible characters.
[/list]

Project Zomboid 42.21.0, single-player. Workshop requires ZombieBuddy 2.3.3 or newer with its one-time loader setup. Use Workshop or standalone, one copy at a time.

